bra on 0 generators is the 3-element? No—it is the lattice of ... known: F_0 is infinite? Actually free Heyting algebra on 0 generators is the Jankov-related; it's the 2-element algebra? Free algebra on zero generators: its elements are constants 0 and 1 only, since no generators; the terms are built from 0,1 with operations, which collapse to {0,1}. So F_0 = 2, which is Sub(1) of Set. F_1 is infinite (Rieger–Nishimura), with countably many elements, plus it's not complete. F_2 is infinite too, has 2^{...}, and F_n for n≥3 is infinite.

